{"seq":2,"slug":"clustering-methods","title":"聚类方法 SwAV 与 DINO","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/self-supervised-contrastive/non-contrastive/clustering-methods","wordCount":1563,"readingTime":7,"html":"<h1 id=\"聚类方法-swav-与-dino\">聚类方法 SwAV 与 DINO</h1><p>对比学习逐对地比较样本，而人类认知更像聚类——我们把世界归成「猫、车、树」这样的类别，而不是记住每两个物体之间的相似度。SwAV 和 DINO 把这个直觉变成方法：不再比较单个样本对，而是让同一图的不同视角被分到同一组「原型」或匹配同一个软分布。这条聚类路线不仅规避了对比学习的假负样本问题，还意外地让 ViT 学出了带语义的注意力图，成为后来视觉基础模型的直接前身。这一篇讲这两个关键方法。</p>\n<h2 id=\"核心概念\">核心概念</h2><p>聚类式自监督的统一思想是：用一组可学习的「原型」（prototypes，类似聚类中心）作为中介。不直接拉近两个视角的特征，而是要求两个视角对原型的「分配」（assignment）一致。SwAV 用在线聚类加均衡约束求分配，DINO 用教师网络的软分布当分配目标。两者都通过原型这个中介把对比变成了「预测分配」。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart TD&#10;    A[一张图] --&gt; B[增强视角1 → 特征 z1]&#10;    A --&gt; C[增强视角2 → 特征 z2]&#10;    D[可学习原型 C] --&gt; E[z1 对原型的软分配 q1]&#10;    D --&gt; F[z2 对原型的软分配 q2]&#10;    B --&gt; E&#10;    C --&gt; F&#10;    E --&gt; G[SwAV: Sinkhorn 求均衡分配]&#10;    G --&gt; H[交换预测: 用 q1 预测 z2 的分配,反之亦然]&#10;    F --&gt; H\">flowchart TD\n    A[一张图] --&gt; B[增强视角1 → 特征 z1]\n    A --&gt; C[增强视角2 → 特征 z2]\n    D[可学习原型 C] --&gt; E[z1 对原型的软分配 q1]\n    D --&gt; F[z2 对原型的软分配 q2]\n    B --&gt; E\n    C --&gt; F\n    E --&gt; G[SwAV: Sinkhorn 求均衡分配]\n    G --&gt; H[交换预测: 用 q1 预测 z2 的分配,反之亦然]\n    F --&gt; H</pre><h2 id=\"swav-在线聚类与交换预测\">SwAV：在线聚类与交换预测</h2><p>SwAV（Swapping Assignments between Views）的巧思是「交换预测」（swapped prediction）：用视角 1 的特征去预测视角 2 算出的聚类分配，反过来也一样。如果两个视角真是同一物体，它们的分配应该可以互相预测。损失是交叉熵形式：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">L</mi><mtext>SwAV</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{SwAV}} = \\ell(z_1, q_2) + \\ell(z_2, q_1), \\quad \\ell(z, q) = -\\sum_k q^{(k)} \\log p^{(k)}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">SwAV</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.044em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.044em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:1em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.3521em;vertical-align:-1.3021em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8479em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3021em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.938em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.938em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span></div><p>其中 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p(z)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 是特征对原型的 softmax 分配，<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">q</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span> 是「目标分配」。难点在于：如果直接用 softmax 当目标，所有样本会被分到同一个原型（坍缩）。SwAV 用 Sinkhorn-Knopp 算法在线求解一个带均衡约束的最优传输，强制一个批次的样本被均匀分配到各原型，从约束上防止坍缩。这种均衡约束是聚类方法防坍缩的核心，对应 <a href=\"../foundations/representation-eval\">表示评估与探针</a> 里的均匀性。</p>\n<p>SwAV 还引入了「multi-crop」技巧：除两个标准大裁剪外，再加几个小裁剪一起训练，用很小的额外算力大幅提升性能。multi-crop 后来被几乎所有非对比方法采用，包括 DINO。</p>\n<h2 id=\"dino-自蒸馏与语义注意力\">DINO：自蒸馏与语义注意力</h2><p>DINO（self-DIstillation with NO labels）把 <a href=\"byol-simsiam\">BYOL 与 SimSiam</a> 的「学生追教师」框架和聚类思想融合，并首次在 ViT 上爆发出惊艳效果。它有学生和教师两个网络（教师是学生的 EMA），都输出对一组原型的概率分布，让学生匹配教师的分布：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">L</mi><mtext>DINO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext>teacher</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mtext>student</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{L}_{\\text{DINO}} = -\\sum_k P_{\\text{teacher}}^{(k)} \\log P_{\\text{student}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\">L</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">DINO</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.3521em;vertical-align:-1.3021em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8479em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3021em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3987em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">teacher</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2198em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3013em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3987em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">student</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2198em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3013em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p>DINO 防坍缩不靠 Sinkhorn，而靠教师输出的「中心化加锐化」（centering and sharpening）这一对相反操作：中心化（减去 EMA 均值）防止某个原型主导（避免坍缩到单一原型），锐化（教师用更低温度）防止分布退化成均匀（避免坍缩到均匀分布）。两者一推一拉维持平衡。</p>\n<p>DINO 最著名的发现是：在 ViT 上自监督训练后，[CLS] token 的自注意力图无需任何标注就清晰地分割出图中的前景物体——自监督意外地学到了物体的语义边界。这个性质让 DINO 的特征在 kNN 检索、分割、检测上都极强，也是它成为基础模型前身的原因。</p>\n<h2 id=\"两类聚类方法对照\">两类聚类方法对照</h2><p>下表对照 SwAV 与 DINO 的关键设计：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>维度</th>\n<th>SwAV</th>\n<th>DINO</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>中介</td>\n<td>在线聚类原型</td>\n<td>教师软分布原型</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>目标分配来源</td>\n<td>Sinkhorn 最优传输</td>\n<td>教师网络（EMA）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>防坍缩机制</td>\n<td>均衡约束（Sinkhorn）</td>\n<td>中心化 + 锐化</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>是否用教师网络</td>\n<td>否</td>\n<td>是</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>multi-crop</td>\n<td>首创</td>\n<td>沿用</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>标志性效果</td>\n<td>高效、追平监督</td>\n<td>ViT 涌现语义注意力</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>两者的共性是用原型当中介把样本级对比抽象成簇级匹配，从而天然规避 <a href=\"../contrastive/negatives-augmentation\">负样本与数据增强</a> 里讨论的假负样本——同类样本被分到同簇，不会被互相推远。差异在防坍缩的具体手段：SwAV 靠优化约束，DINO 靠统计后处理。</p>\n<h2 id=\"通向基础模型\">通向基础模型</h2><p>DINO 的成功直接催生了 DINOv2（2023）和 DINOv3（2025）。DINOv2 用海量策展数据把这套配方扩展成通用视觉特征，DINOv3 进一步推到七十亿参数、十七亿图片，并用 Gram Anchoring 解决长训练下稠密特征退化问题（来源：Meta AI，<a href=\"https://ai.meta.com/blog/dinov3-self-supervised-vision-model/\">DINOv3</a>，2025）。这条从 DINO 到 DINOv3 的演进，是 <a href=\"../applications/scaling-foundation\">扩展与基础模型</a> 的核心线索。</p>\n<h2 id=\"常见误区\">常见误区</h2><p>聚类路线的两个防坍缩机制各有其误用方式：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>误区</th>\n<th>后果</th>\n<th>纠正</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>SwAV 直接用 softmax 当目标</td>\n<td>所有样本被分到同一原型，发生坍缩</td>\n<td>目标分配必须经 Sinkhorn 均衡约束求解，不能直接 softmax</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>把中心化或锐化单独使用</td>\n<td>单个操作会把分布推向另一种坍缩</td>\n<td>中心化防「坍缩到单原型」、锐化防「坍缩到均匀」，须成对使用</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>认为原型数越多越好</td>\n<td>原型过多时分配稀疏，均衡约束难生效</td>\n<td>原型数要与批次大小、任务粒度匹配</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>把聚类当作纯工程技巧</td>\n<td>忽略它规避假负样本的结构性优势</td>\n<td>理解「簇级匹配替代样本级对比」这一根源，才能用好它</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一个值得记住的事实：这两种方法的防坍缩手段性质不同——SwAV 靠优化阶段的约束，DINO 靠输出的统计后处理，这决定了它们对超参的敏感点也不同。</p>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>聚类方法用可学习「原型」当中介，让两个视角的分配一致，把样本级对比抽象成簇级匹配，天然规避假负样本。</li>\n<li>SwAV 用交换预测加 Sinkhorn 均衡约束防坍缩，首创 multi-crop 小裁剪技巧；目标分配来自最优传输。</li>\n<li>DINO 用学生追 EMA 教师的自蒸馏，靠教师输出的中心化加锐化防坍缩；在 ViT 上涌现出无监督语义分割的注意力图。</li>\n<li>两者差异在防坍缩手段（优化约束 vs 统计后处理）；DINO 这条线直接演进出 DINOv2/v3 视觉基础模型。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"聚类方法 SwAV 与 DINO","id":"聚类方法-swav-与-dino"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"SwAV：在线聚类与交换预测","id":"swav-在线聚类与交换预测"},{"level":2,"text":"DINO：自蒸馏与语义注意力","id":"dino-自蒸馏与语义注意力"},{"level":2,"text":"两类聚类方法对照","id":"两类聚类方法对照"},{"level":2,"text":"通向基础模型","id":"通向基础模型"},{"level":2,"text":"常见误区","id":"常见误区"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"BYOL 与 SimSiam","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/self-supervised-contrastive/non-contrastive/byol-simsiam"},"next":{"title":"掩码建模 MAE","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/self-supervised-contrastive/non-contrastive/masked-modeling"}}